+  str(filterWords(.IntSeq, W))
+with the deliberately false
+  str(seqConcat(filterWords(.IntSeq, W), iCons(120, .IntSeq)))
+which demands an extra trailing ASCII `x`.
+
+SATISFYING COUNTEREXAMPLE:
+For W = ["aa", "bbb", "cccc"], the precondition holds and actual result is
+"aa bbb", while the mutated destination demands "aa bbbx".
+
+COMMAND (cwd=/tmp/audit-work/143):
+kprove spec-vacuity.k --definition verification-kompiled \
+  --spec-module SPEC-VACUITY \
+  --claims SPEC-VACUITY.loop-invariant,SPEC-VACUITY.words-in-sentence-correct \
+  --trusted SPEC-VACUITY.loop-invariant --output pretty
+EXIT STATUS: 1 (expected)
+RELEVANT OUTPUT:
+kore-exec: Warning (WarnStuckClaimState):
+  The configuration's term unifies with the destination's term, but the
+  implication check between the conditions has failed.
+Residual obligation:
+  filterWords(.IntSeq, W)
+  #Equals
+  seqConcat(filterWords(.IntSeq, W), iCons(120, .IntSeq))
+Residual final result:
+  <k> str(filterWords(.IntSeq, W)) ~> .K </k>
+[Error] Prover: backend terminated because the configuration cannot be
+rewritten further.
+
+The mutation parsed and reached the end-to-end final state; failure was the
+intended unmet result equality, not a parser/build/timeout error.
